1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%B6sta_Malcolm_Lillieh%C3%B6%C3%B6k
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%B6sta_Lillieh%C3%B6%C3%B6k_%281884%E2%80%931974%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustaf Malcolm "Gösta" Lilliehöök (25 May 1884 – 18 November 1974) was a Swedish officer and modern pentathlete. He won a gold medal in the first contested modern pentathlon at the Olympic Games in 1912.
2 CONT
2 CONT Career
2 CONT
2 CONT Lilliehöök was born on 25 May 1884 in Stockholm, Sweden, the son of First Marshal of the Court Carl Malcolm Lilliehöök and his wife Anna Ekelund. He was commissioned as an officer in Svea Artillery Regiment in 1906 with the rank o
2 CONC f acting sub-lieutenant (underlöjtnant). Lilliehöök was promoted to lieutenant in 1910 and to captain in 1918 after which he was placed in the reserve.
2 CONT
2 CONT He won a gold medal in the first contested modern pentathlon at the Olympic Games in 1912. He later became one of the first five employees of the national Swedish radio.
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal life
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1922, Lilliehöök married Anna de Fine Blauw (born 1891), the daughter of the artist Dick Blauw and Marie de Fine Beyer.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://slektenbeyer.com/showmedia.php?mediaID=3189
