2 CONT
2 CONT Adrianus van Bergen den 20sten Juni 1860 gehuwd met Wilhelmina Dorothea Wichelhousen, Holland. Gereisd van Holland met het schip “Agatha Maria”. Kaptein: Van der Ryst
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Ons eerste kind zijnde een zoontje – 23.3.1861 morgens ten 8 ure te Franschoek, gedoopt Louis Cornelius doch herdoopt in zijns vaders swaar siekbed met die naam Adrianus Louis Cornelius door ds. PN Ham. '''2. Ons tweede kind ee
2 CONC n dochtertje is geboren 31 October 1862’s middag om 4 ure te Franschoek en gedoopt door ds PN Daneel, Wilhelmina Dorothea gestorven 6.3. 1863 te Franschoek.''' 3. Ons derde kind, een zoontje is geboren 6 April 1864’s avonds om 9 ½
2 CONC  ure te Malmesbury en gedoopt door ds. Moorrees, Wilhelm Andries 5. Ons vijfde kind, een dochtertje, is geboren 24.5.1867 en gedoopt door ds Van der Lingen, Maria Cornelia te Paarl. 6. Ons sesde kind, een dogtertje, is geboren op 
2 CONC Kleintoren in de Hantam distrik, Colesberg , 9.3.1869’s avonds om 10 ½ ure en gedoopt 5 April door dr. D Postma op Springfontein genaamd Engelina Wilhelmina(Moeder van JF van Wyk) 7. Ons zevende kind, een zoontje, is geboren 11 Ja
2 CONC nuarie 1871’s avonds om 11 ¼ ure op Poortje distrik Filippolis, OVS en gedoopt Johannes Cornelis door ds. Fraser te Filippolis 12.3.1871
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSFQ-S9K5-H?view=index&personArk=%2Fark%3A%2F61903%2F1%3A1%3A622L-K9ND&action=view Birth and baptism] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Name	Engelina Wilhelmina Dorothea Van Bergen
2 CONT Birth Date	
2 CONT
2 CONT 30 October 1862
2 CONT
2 CONT Parent Name	Adrianus Van Bergen
2 CONT Second Parent's Name	Wilhelmia Dorothea Wechelhausen
2 CONT Event Type	Baptism
2 CONT Event Date	
2 CONT
2 CONT 23 November 1862
2 CONT
2 CONT The Church called Fransch Hoek 1844 --  https://www.familysearch.org/search/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSFQ-S9KK-D?view=index&action=view
2 CONT
2 CONT Another copy 30 October 1862 --- https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSK6-9S8X-H?view=index&personArk=%2Fark%3A%2F61903%2F1%3A1%3A6231-1LYC&action=view
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT HOWEVER NO Franschhoek before 1881 :
2 CONT
2 CONT Franschhoek, the town, first began to emerge as a little one-street dorp in the 1820s. It was simply the “dorp”, without any name tag. Only in 1881 when the area became a municipality did the village, then called Roubaix Dorp, cha
2 CONC nge its name to Fransche Hoek and become a small town. Prior to this when referring to the broader area in conversation, some would refer to “le Quartier Francais” or “Le Coin Francais”. The village first took shape in 1832 with t
2 CONC he establishment of a chapel. Notably one of the chief arguments for establishing the chapel and later a church which was the cornerstone of starting the “kerksdorp”, was that it was needed for the farm workers of colour who had n
2 CONC o means to travel to church services in Paarl. This “kerksdorp” acquired the name Roubaix Dorp after a petition in 1859 by villagers led by FCM Voight, a government teacher, to name their town after the MP for Paarl, Mr de Roubaix
2 CONC . There was some division in the town over this move, but it would take 30 more years to change the name to Franschhoek.
