0 @N6000000000113827891@ NOTE [Shawns.ged.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT The first Höegh who came to Norway from Denmark was a minister and professor who was a younger brother of Ole Höegh Gulberg.  There was also a third brother.  Maybe the minister got his job and professor title from his brother and
1 CONC  was sent to Skedsmo? (can not clearly decipher place) in Norway, while his brother Ole Höegh-Gulberg- very intelligent and highly placed in the Danish government-was conspiring  wthi Struensee (see Danish history).  After having 
1 CONC ruled in Denmark for many years he was demoted to ?stiftamtmann? (high functionary) in Aarhus.  One of the minister?s many sons was sent there from Norway to study and lived at his famous uncle?s house.  The Danish side of the fam
1 CONC ily were nobles.  Young Höegh  who went to Aarhus to study later became  ?fogd? ( High functionary) in Solør (eastern Norway) and burned to death with some of his family during the big fire in Grue Church.  He was your great-great
1 CONC -great-great grandfather, Shawn.  Fogd Höegh had many children.  One wasOle Rüs Höegh who became State Architect in Bergen and was also a symphony conductor.  When he was 20, he got a job as assistant to architect Lindslow who bui
1 CONC lt the castle in Christiania (Now Olso).  Later he moved to Halden and drew the church in the center of town.  In Halden he married into a commercial family by the name of Selmer and moved to Bergen.  His wife- your great-great-gr
1 CONC eat grandmother was the sister of Secretary of State Selmer - he was sentenced to death by the Supreme Court in 1884.
1 CONT
1 CONT Minister Höegh who came from Denmark in the 1700?s
1 CONT begat
1 CONT Fogd Höegh who burned to death in Solør.
